# Build context is the repo root for all JS app images, so this is the ONLY ignore file
# those builds read: Docker takes .dockerignore from the context root (or a
# <Dockerfile>.dockerignore beside the Dockerfile), never a .dockerignore beside it.
# check:docker holds the .env rule and fails on an ignore file nothing reads. Keep it lean.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/.turbo
.git
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
**/.env
**/__pycache__
*.tsbuildinfo

# Python venvs — gitignored, copied into NO image, but the build context is the repo
# root, so without this every service build tars them to the daemon.
**/.venv

# The music embedder is deliberately outside the pnpm workspace and copied into
# NO image, but it holds ~2.8 GB (venv, CLAP export, index, rendered output) that
# would otherwise ship to the daemon on every root-context build — the same cost
# the venv block above exists to stop.
music/

# The native shells build in their own image (native/android/Dockerfile) or on the desktop,
# never inside an app image. Keep their Gradle caches and outputs off the daemon.
native/android/
native/desktop/out/
